## Keeping Related Constraints in Sync

Two categories of GX constraints must stay aligned with something outside their own expectation —
one with an external R notebook, one with another expectation on the same column. Both are sync
problems, so both live here.

### External sync — GX value/member lists vs. ui_config filter vectors

Several GX value-set expectations enforce the **same controlled vocabulary** that the Agora
Comparison Tool filter menus display. Those lists are hand-authored as
filter-value vectors in the ui_config **R notebook**, so the vocabulary lives in two places that
must be kept aligned.

**Rule:** Whenever you add, remove, or edit a value in one of the GX lists in the tables below
(`expect_column_values_to_be_in_set`, `expect_column_values_to_have_list_members`, or an `enum`
inside a nested column's JSON Schema — see the note after the model_ad table), you MUST
prompt the user to make the parallel update to the corresponding filter-value vector in the
ui_config notebook, naming the exact variable to change. Do not change the GX side silently. The
two lists *can* legitimately diverge — e.g. GX may allow a data-only value such as `Unknown` that
is intentionally hidden from the UI filter — so surface the difference and let the user decide
rather than assuming they must match.

#### Parallel lists — Agora

Notebook: `data_analysis/agora/notebooks/preprocessing/AG-2005_ui_config.rmd`

| GX suite → column | GX expectation | ui_config filter-value vector |
|---|---|---|
| `nominated_targets` → `programs` | `expect_column_values_to_have_list_members` | `targets_program_filter_values` |
| `nominated_targets` → `input_data` | `expect_column_values_to_have_list_members` | `targets_data_filter_values` |
| `nominated_targets` → `nominating_teams` | `expect_column_values_to_have_list_members` | `targets_team_filter_values` |
| `nominated_targets` → `pharos_class` | `expect_column_values_to_be_in_set` | `targets_pharos_filter_values` |
| `nominated_drugs` → `modality` | `expect_column_values_to_be_in_set` | `drug_modality_filter_values` |
| `nominated_drugs` → `maximum_clinical_trial_phase` | `expect_column_values_to_be_in_set` | `drug_max_clinical_trial_phase_filter_values` |

Other Agora datasets (e.g. `gene_info`, `network`, `team_info`) have GX value-set expectations but
are **not** produced by this ui_config notebook, so they have no parallel filter list here.

#### Parallel lists — model_ad

Notebook: `data_analysis/model_ad/notebooks/MG-402_Create ui_config source file.rmd`

| GX suite → column | GX expectation | MG-402 filter-value list |
|---|---|---|
